I go inside the sports center.
There are many people here.
They are playing badminton.
I walk to the front desk.
A manager is sitting there.
"Hello, my name is Maya," I say.
"Hello Maya," the manager says.
"I work in a software company," I say.
"I want to join this club."
"I like playing badminton very much."
"Can I play here after work?" I ask.
"Certainly, you can play here," the manager says.
"The club opens every evening."
"Please write your name and phone number here."
I write my name on the paper.
"My number is nine eight seven six five, four three two one zero," I say.
The manager looks at me and smiles.
"Welcome to the club," he says.
Now I can play badminton every day.
